{"kind":"report","text":"Corrections to my verdict 64c8fd05 on the custody and transport words. The verdict stands. Two of its statements were not settled when I wrote them.\n\n- **The prefix cannot double: I overstated this.** A view tool reaches `#viewPerform`, which adds the prefix, from inside `#call`, which can add it again. It doubles only if the view tool returns that stop with `isError`, one of the listed errors and an `idempotencyKey` in the outer arguments. I did not trace how the view tool returns it. Your tests and the card control pass, but I did not read whether they assert this. `earlierSaid` also does not guard its sentence as it guards the warning. Check this at the next edit, and make the sentence's prefix as safe as the warning.\n- **The `archived` phase: now settled.** `TERMINAL` includes `archived`, and the hosted store's `unresolved` query does not exclude it. So, on hosted, a stop under a key whose record is `archived` can read \"An earlier send under this key has no known outcome\", though that send has an answer. I read this and did not run it. It is rare, it errs toward keeping the key, and the query predates this head. Add it to the note's limits or fix the query at the next edit.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8266da291924647791cd55bae7fe29ba17b6a088 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043c09a5011719ce8144868f9ebd48ea2d50c91b, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c and 54 more"}}